# Rank 1099 / CVE-2022-31121: Hyperledger Fabric's orderer treated any
# non-Submit gRPC StepRequest as a consensus message, so a request with
# neither oneof case set reached DispatchConsensus with a nil consensus
# request and crashed the node deeper in the dispatch path (CWE-20). The
# generated oneof accessor returns nil unless its case was set:
#
#   func (m *StepRequest) GetConsensusRequest() *ConsensusRequest {
#       if x, ok := m.GetPayload().(*StepRequest_ConsensusRequest); ok {
#           return x.ConsensusRequest
#       }
#       return nil
#   }
#
# The fix requires GetConsensusRequest() to be non-nil before dispatching
# and returns an error otherwise. Note the fix re-calls the accessor inline
# at the guarded dispatch site, so the call shape is identical in both
# revisions and only the enclosing guard differs.
#
# ATTENTION, not mechanical, re-measured at scanner d0cae877d. The generic
# vocabulary for this class exists but reaches no Go code:
# code.NullableDeref's only Go binding is hardcoded to one free5gc function
# (nullableDeref39, bindings/packages/go/m39efcd29.vyql), and
# code.UncheckedNullableResultDeref (VYQL-MEM-018) fires only from the C and
# C++ extractors' analysis.nullable_result.unchecked_deref fact
# (ccUncheckedNullableResultDerefObservations, c.go:3003), which models a
# local assignment then a member dereference -- here the accessor result is
# never assigned or dereferenced locally; it is passed inline as an
# argument. vyql match on the real service.go labels no source, sink or
# control, and three scans of the orderer subtree per revision report 13
# findings each with none in common/cluster/service.go. An exhaustive grep
# of the whole tree finds exactly one unguarded GetConsensusRequest flowing
# into DispatchConsensus -- service.go:96, the vulnerability; every other
# occurrence is nil-guarded or is the vendored definition.
#
# Three function-context probes on the real cluster package at both
# revisions locate what a presence binding could key on:
#   - callPath contains DispatchConsensus + GetConsensusRequest fires on
#     both revisions (1/1);
#   - adding `not (node.context.binary contains "!=nil")` fires on neither
#     (0/0): the vulnerable function's own submitReq != nil guard -- on the
#     OTHER oneof case -- satisfies the blanket negation, and a
#     discriminator dispatch always carries one guarded accessor;
#   - only negating the fix's own guard variable (`nsensusReq!=nil`)
#     discriminates (1/0), which is the fixing commit's layout, not a
#     generic condition.
# The missing fact is a join between "local assigned from accessor X" and
# "nil guard on that local": goAtomToken returns "" for every CallExpr
# except len() (internal/extract/frontend/golang/golang.go:1368), so
# `consensusReq := request.GetConsensusRequest()` emits no assign: token,
# and presence predicates cannot unify a variable name across assign: and
# binary: clauses regardless. That is the "a check cannot be attributed to
# the value it is applied to" defect in ENGINE-GAPS.md (measured instances
# 1420/1427/1430), restated for this nilness-guard family by rank 1885's
# branch-correlated nilness entry with its Go comma-ok instance. Design
# work on the concept and the guard analysis together, not a port. Both
# tests below pin the miss against both memory rules.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-not-mechanical

test "rank1099: a non-submit request is dispatched as consensus with no nil check"
  lang go
  file orderer/common/cluster/service.go
  reject VYQL-MEM-006
  reject VYQL-MEM-018
  code
  ```
  package cluster

  func (s *Service) handleMessage(stream StepStream, addr string, exp *certificateExpirationCheck) error {
    request, err := stream.Recv()
    if err != nil {
      return err
    }

    if submitReq := request.GetSubmitRequest(); submitReq != nil {
      return s.handleSubmit(submitReq, stream, addr)
    }

    // Else, it's a consensus message.
    return s.Dispatcher.DispatchConsensus(stream.Context(), request.GetConsensusRequest())
  }
  ```

test "rank1099: the fixed revision requires the consensus field to be populated"
  lang go
  file orderer/common/cluster/service.go
  reject VYQL-MEM-006
  reject VYQL-MEM-018
  code
  ```
  package cluster

  func (s *Service) handleMessage(stream StepStream, addr string, exp *certificateExpirationCheck) error {
    request, err := stream.Recv()
    if err != nil {
      return err
    }

    if submitReq := request.GetSubmitRequest(); submitReq != nil {
      return s.handleSubmit(submitReq, stream, addr)
    } else if consensusReq := request.GetConsensusRequest(); consensusReq != nil {
      return s.Dispatcher.DispatchConsensus(stream.Context(), request.GetConsensusRequest())
    }

    return errors.Errorf("message is neither a Submit nor a Consensus request")
  }
  ```
